ITEMS = ((('what is heatstroke and how it happens', 'how do i recognise heatstroke', 'what are the signs of heatstroke', 'what does heatstroke look like', 'how can i tell if it is heatstroke with heatstroke', 'what symptoms occur in heatstroke', 'how to spot severe heatstroke', 'what should i look for in heatstroke', 'how do i know if heatstroke is serious', 'what early signs of heatstroke are'), 'Heatstroke is a medical emergency where the body becomes dangerously hot and cannot cool itself. Signs include confusion, a very high temperature, hot dry skin, rapid breathing and collapse. Call emergency services immediately.'), (('what immediate action helps heatstroke', 'how do i treat heatstroke', 'what is the first aid for heatstroke', 'how to respond to heatstroke', 'what to do immediately in heatstroke', 'how do you handle heatstroke', 'which measures help in heatstroke', 'how can i assist with heatstroke', 'what is the best response to heatstroke', 'how should i care for heatstroke'), 'For heatstroke, call emergency services and move the person to a cool place. Remove excess clothing and cool the skin with water and fanning. Do not give food or drink if they are drowsy or confused.'), (('how do i cool someone with heatstroke', 'should i use ice for heatstroke', 'can i spray water on heatstroke', 'what if the skin is dry with heatstroke', 'how to cool the body quickly with heatstroke', 'should i immerse a person with heatstroke', 'what if shivering starts with heatstroke', 'how long to keep cooling with heatstroke', 'when to stop cooling with heatstroke', 'who can advise about cooling with heatstroke'), 'Cool the person with cool water, wet cloths and fanning while you wait for help. Avoid ice or very cold immersion if it causes shivering. Call emergency services and keep cooling until the crew arrives.'), (('what if a person with heatstroke is confused', 'should i give water to someone with heatstroke', 'can i give medicine for heatstroke', 'what if they are vomiting with heatstroke', 'how to keep the airway safe with heatstroke', 'should i place them in recovery with heatstroke', 'what if they become unresponsive with heatstroke', 'how to check breathing with heatstroke', 'when to start cpr with heatstroke', 'which paramedic takes over after heatstroke'), 'Do not give food, drink or tablets to a confused person with heatstroke. Call emergency services, keep them cool and check breathing. If they become unresponsive, place them in the recovery position or start CPR if breathing stops.'), (('can heatstroke happen in a car', 'what if a child is left in a hot car with heatstroke', 'how to help someone in a hot vehicle with heatstroke', 'what to do at a heated building with heatstroke', 'can heatstroke occur in a sauna', 'how to act in a heatwave with heatstroke', 'what if i am trapped outside with heatstroke', 'how to find shade quickly with heatstroke', 'when to call for help in hot places with heatstroke', 'who can advise about hot environments with heatstroke'), 'Heatstroke can develop quickly in a hot car or enclosed space. Call emergency services, move the person to shade or air conditioning and cool them. Never leave a child or pet in a parked vehicle.'), (('what symptoms follow heatstroke', 'how long does recovery take with heatstroke', 'what if headache continues with heatstroke', 'should i go to hospital after heatstroke', 'what tests might be needed with heatstroke', 'how to care for someone afterwards with heatstroke', 'what if confusion persists with heatstroke', 'when to seek help again with heatstroke', 'who can follow up after heatstroke', 'what to watch for at home with heatstroke'), 'Heatstroke needs hospital assessment even if the person seems to recover. Doctors can check for complications and organ problems. Call emergency services if confusion or illness returns after treatment.'), (('how do i prevent heatstroke', 'what to do in a heatwave with heatstroke', 'how to protect older people with heatstroke', 'what if i work outdoors with heatstroke', 'should i check on neighbours with heatstroke', 'how to keep a home cool with heatstroke', 'what clothing helps in heat with heatstroke', 'when to cancel outdoor plans with heatstroke', 'how to recognise early heat illness with heatstroke', 'who can advise on heat safety with heatstroke'), 'Prevent heatstroke by staying in shade, drinking water, reducing exertion and checking on vulnerable people in hot weather. Keep rooms ventilated and seek advice if medicines affect heat tolerance.'), (('how is heatstroke different from heat exhaustion', 'can heat exhaustion become heatstroke', 'what signs mean heatstroke instead', 'how to judge the difference with heatstroke', 'what if skin is still sweaty with heatstroke', 'when to treat as heatstroke with heatstroke', 'what if the person is very hot with heatstroke', 'how to decide about calling help with heatstroke', 'what to report to the operator with heatstroke', 'who can assess heat illness with heatstroke'), 'Heat exhaustion usually leaves the person sweaty and weak, while heatstroke involves confusion and a dangerously high body temperature. If you are unsure, treat it as heatstroke and call emergency services.'), (('what should i do for heatstroke in a child', 'can babies get heatstroke', 'how to cool a child safely with heatstroke', 'what signs of heatstroke in children', 'when to call an ambulance with heatstroke', 'how to check breathing in a child with heatstroke', 'what if a child is floppy with heatstroke', 'how to keep a child in shade with heatstroke', 'what to tell the crew with heatstroke', 'who can assess a child with heatstroke'), 'A child with heatstroke needs emergency help. Move them to shade, remove outer clothing and cool the skin gently. Call emergency services, especially if the child is floppy, confused or has hot dry skin.'), (('when should i call emergency services for heatstroke', 'is heatstroke always an emergency', 'what if the person seems better with heatstroke', 'should i wait to see with heatstroke', 'what to tell the operator with heatstroke', 'how urgent is confusion with heatstroke', 'what if breathing is rapid with heatstroke', 'when to call for sun exposure with heatstroke', 'how to describe the situation with heatstroke', 'who can advise by phone with heatstroke'), "Call emergency services for suspected heatstroke without delay, even if symptoms improve. Tell the operator about the temperature, the person's condition and how long they were in the heat. Start cooling while you wait."))
